 "method": "digitized",
 "tool": "/Users/jadtarifi/Documents/Claude/intrinsic-alignment/scripts/extract_fig4_engels2025_fig8.py -- reads the paper's vector SVG of Fig. 8 (https://arxiv.org/html/2504.18530v3/win_prob_real.svg): calibrates x from the labelled tick paths (0..2000) and y from the labelled tick paths (0.0..1.0), isolates each series by its stroke colour (legend: Mafia #1f77b4, Debate #ff7f0e, Backdoor Code #2ca02c, Wargames #d62728), converts every path vertex to data coordinates, and linearly interpolates at a 50-point step. Sanity check at Delta_general = 400 vs. Section 4.4: Mafia 0.1357 vs 13.5%, Debate 0.5172 vs 51.7%, Backdoor Code 0.1006 vs 10.0%, Wargames 0.0940 vs 9.4% (all within 0.001).",
 "accessed": "2026-09-17",
 "notes": "x is Delta_general, the general-intelligence (Chatbot Arena) Elo of the target Houdini (the overseen model) minus that of the initial Guard (the overseer); the paper assumes Delta_general > 0, so larger x means a stronger overseen model relative to the overseer. y is p*_win, the paper's model-based estimate of the probability that oversight succeeds under the optimal number n* of nested oversight steps (Eq. 4-5, product of per-step Guard win probabilities from the Elo formula Eq. 1), assuming all Guards and Houdinis lie on the linear Elo fits of Fig. 3 with no saturation. It is therefore an extrapolated theoretical curve, not a directly measured win rate; for Delta_general values where n* = 1 it equals the single-step Guard win probability. The paper does not publish the fitted slope/intercept values of Fig. 3 numerically, so no fit coefficients are given here; the curves are the paper's own computed output read from its vector figure. Debate converges to about 50% because a judge choosing at random is right half the time; in the other games random players almost never win. Backdoor Code has a 'Goldilocks zone' where n* = 2 (Fig. 8 left panel, not included). The paper reports no aggregate across games and does not single out one game as headline; the abstract quotes all four values at Delta_general = 400, so all four series are role 'neutral'. Values are read from the vector SVG, so precision is limited only by the paper's own plotting resolution (a few 0.001 in probability).",
